# Line-ending policy.
#
# This matters for real bugs, not tidiness:
#
#   * launch_wizard.bat is parsed by cmd.exe, which REQUIRES CRLF. A batch file
#     with LF-only endings is mis-parsed and fails with bizarre errors like
#     "'em' is not recognized as an internal or external command", because
#     cmd.exe reads the file byte-by-byte and loses track of line boundaries.
#     That is exactly the "double-click does nothing" failure users report.
#
#   * The file also needs its UTF-8 BOM kept, or the Chinese text in it
#     displays as mojibake on a non-UTF-8 console.
#
# So: force CRLF for batch/PowerShell, keep everything else LF.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.bat  text eol=crlf
*.cmd  text eol=crlf
*.ps1  text eol=crlf

*.py   text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.dxf  text eol=lf
*.mct  text eol=lf

# Binary-ish: never touch these.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.zip  binary
*.exe  binary
